MAN: Mr. Cho.

262
00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:48.801
Mr. Cho.

263
00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:52.089
♪♪

264
00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.244
To see... Kara Powell.

265
00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.967
MAN: One moment, please.

266
00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:04.206
Your pass code
is 7-8-5-star-9-5.

267
00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.486
[ Beep ]

268
00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.211
[ Elevator doors close,
whirring ]

269
00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:11.204
♪♪

270
00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:13.601
RAY: You expected me to create
a dedicated office mobile app

271
00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:14.807
with servers that run
on hamster wheels.

272
00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.002
Ray, stop talking.

273
00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:19.686
If I hear another
whining excuse from you,

274
00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:20.961
I'll make sure
you're back to building

275
00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.009
porn-site banner ads by lunch.

276
00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.685
Do you understand me?
[ Knock on door ]

277
00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.410
RAY: Yes, fine.

278
00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.722
THE SIREN: So stop playing
video games in your troll cave

279
00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:32.407
and get the interoffice apps
updated ASAP, okay, sweetie?

280
00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.329
Okay. Thank you so much.
Bye-bye.

281
00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.568
[ Beep ]
Asshole.

282
00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:39.007
- What I can do for you?
- That's a nice mug.

283
00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:40.366
Where'd you get it?

284
00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:42.648
I told my assistant
to get me one.

285
00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.926
And where did she get it?

286
00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:45.650
Meg!

287
00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:49.247
Derek here wants to know
where you got the mug.

288
00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.243
From a kitchen downstairs.

289
00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.210
Okay. And why did you
choose that one?

290
00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.771
MEG: Because the other ones
were filthy.

291
00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.405
DEREK: And why do you think
this one wasn't?

292
00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:59.244
MEG:
Because the maid cleaned it.

293
00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:03.041
DEREK: Incorrect. I cleaned this
mug because this mug is mine.

294
00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.770
And what's mine is mine.

295
00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:06.763
And what's yours is yours.

296
00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.285
You're getting to a point.

297
00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.044
Vanda Corp is your client.

298
00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.929
That blood's on your hands.

299
00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.082
Oh. Oh, so now
you want to share.

300
00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.607
DEREK:
I can't share what isn't mine.

301
00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.081
Vanda Corp has filed
more than 100 account cases

302
00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:20.685
through us
in the last two years.

303
00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:22.604
Well, then I hope they have
a good case manager.

304
00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.649
You mean managers.

305
00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.610
No one can work a client
that big without delegating.

306
00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:30.161
And according to the annual
work distribution sheet...

307
00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.687
That hasn't been
updated in years.

308
00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.561
...one of Vanda Corp's complaint
cases was assigned...

309
00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:37.767
[ Beep ]

310
00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.691
...to you.

311
00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.484
File 45A.

312
00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:45.007
♪♪

313
00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.242
[ Scoffs ]
I'm being set up.

314
00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:52.088
♪♪

315
00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.084
Wow.
Heads will roll.

316
00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:57.004
This will cost Vanda --

317
00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.446
Give me this.

318
00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.524
♪♪

319
00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:04.081
- This was planted.
- I'll cut you a deal.

320
00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.964
- Plead guilty.
- Not guilty.

321
00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:08.043
The corpse was found
inside your office.

322
00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.447
You knew exactly
where to find it.

323
00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:11.965
Do you want to
take this upstairs?

324
00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.084
Great idea.
Take your file.

325
00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:17.607
♪♪

326
00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.205
THE SIREN:
Want to swipe your key card,

327
00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:20.771
or should I swipe mine?

328
00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:24.123
Oh. Oh, I'm sorry.
I forgot.

329
00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.930
You don't have clearance.

330
00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.845
[ Beeping ]

331
00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.571
My bad.

332
00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.603
Don't you worry, little one.

333
00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.444
Daddy will pay
for abandoning you

334
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.371
and leaving you to die
in that cold, dirty Dumpster.

335
00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.449
No, no.
You died when you drowned

336
00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.011
because Mommy left you
in the bathtub

337
00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.003
while she went shopping
for shoes.

338
00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:47.004
But don't worry.
Daddy will make her pay.

339
00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.288
Too bad Mommy outranks Daddy.

340
00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:50.930
DEREK:
Mommy's a backstabbing bitch.

341
00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:52.889
THE SIREN:
That's why Mommy outranks Daddy.

342
00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.805
[ Elevator bell dings ]

343
00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:57.530
- Brenda, what's his mood?
- BRENDA: He's drawing.

344
00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.887
Oh, shit.

345
00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:04.165
John Towers, capital "T" in TSC,
king of the castle,

346
00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:07.244
top of the food chain,
and total fucking maniac --

347
00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:10.449
you know, your typical
American success story.

348
00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:13.331
Did I mention that he also
dabbles in the fine arts?

349
00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.691
Tell me what you see here.

350
00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:23.287
I see that those soldiers'
lives are in danger, sir.

351
00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.686
Do you think they'll make it?

352
00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:26.251
No, sir.
The fuse is too short.

353
00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:27.930
It's too late to run.

354
00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:29.684
And what do you think
they should be doing instead?

355
00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:30.966
May I, sir?

356
00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:32.121
Hmm.

357
00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.322
[ Tablet thuds ]

358
00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:37.768
[ Pen scratching ]

359
00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:40.048
[ Pen thuds ]

360
00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:43.967
So simple and yet so effective.

361
00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.360
Can you see it, Derek?

362
00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:48.046
Can you see the solution
to our problem here?

363
00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.521
I think you mean her problem
because she was the one that --

364
00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:53.001
[ Tablet thuds ]
Give me the file.

365
00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:55.288
This is our bomb.

366
00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.681
The fuse is already burning.

367
00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:00.889
So should we run
like cowards and die?

368
00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.769
We are brave, sir.

369
00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.402
I'm so glad you said that,
because any second now,

370
00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.847
Vanda Corp is gonna
find out about this mess,

371
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.651
and I'm gonna need some scalps.

372
00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.724
So, who dropped the ball?

373
00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:17.201
I hate pointing fingers,
but may I suggest

374
00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:20.170
you check the annual
work distribution sheet?

375
00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:23.722
Someone cooked
the fucking worksheet.

376
00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.689
Sir.

377
00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.968
Go on.

378
00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:31.090
Have you noticed that whenever
there's a problem like this,

379
00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.882
it's almost always
the same soldier involved?

380
00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:40.090
Because down in the trenches,
we have all noticed.

381
00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:43.722
And we wonder if discharging
this problem soldier

382
00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:46.451
might be the solution
to preventing this kind of mess

383
00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.410
from ever happening again.

384
00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:50.925
And who would that be?

385
00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:52.127
May I?

386
00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:58.930
♪♪

387
00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.851
[ Marker squeaking ]

388
00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.405
[ Cap clicks ]

389
00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:08.441
♪♪

390
00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:12.286
Thank you, Derek.
You can leave.

391
00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.771
Let's discuss.

392
00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:14.887
Yes, sir.

393
00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.530
- Leave.

394
00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:22.568
♪♪

395
00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:24.563
[ Footsteps depart ]

396
00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:30.011
♪♪

397
00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:33.323
[ Elevator bell dings ]

398
00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.811
You got a sec?

399
00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:40.410
♪♪

400
00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:48.001
Ahhh-ummmm.

401
00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:51.084
♪♪

402
00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:53.641
Nothing like a little
power meditation.

403
00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.561
This one's new.
Declan's walking already?

404
00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:02.482
Wobbling, actually, like you
were last Friday night.

405
00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.011
Thanks for the ride, by the way.

406
00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.924
Thanks for puking in my car.

407
00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.923
That's what friends are for.

408
00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:11.163
So debrief me.
What happened?

409
00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.045
Just found someone else's shit
swept under my carpet.

410
00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:15.884
What kind of shit?

411
00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.122
Vanda Corp shit.

412
00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.448
It's a seven-figure mistake.
I didn't even touch the file.

413
00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.682
Ah, don't sweat it.

414
00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:24.444
Those clowns working Vanda Corp

415
00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.080
are a bunch of
a serial screw-ups.

416
00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:29.527
Look, I realize you might
not want to divulge --

417
00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:32.968
The Siren.

418
00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:37.284
All right. Let's take
a beat to strategize.

419
00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.408
Since the promotion,
you could possibly

420
00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:41.210
be in charge of a case that big

421
00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:44.045
but not big enough
to be untouchable.

422
00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.044
That's why she chose you.
You're the perfect fall guy.

423
00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:51.000
So before even taking
this upstairs --

424
00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:55.165
You already took this upstairs
and made a mess of things.

425
00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.044
[ Sighs ]

426
00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.406
Fuck

427
00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:01.245
Say I punch a rhino in the face.

428
00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:04.165
Would you call that
brave or stupid?

429
00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:05.890
Brave...

430
00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.923
and stupid.

431
00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.885
See how bravery and stupidity
can overlap?

432
00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.401
Now that you understand that,
let me give her a call

433
00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:15.927
and see if I can't find a way
to cut you a deal.

434
00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:17.809
She already offered me a deal.

435
00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:21.726
I told her to suck it
and that this is war.

436
00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.041
War is over, moron.

437
00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.771
- Come on in, Kara.
- How so?

438
00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:28.810
Natural selection happened.
Pack your shit.

439
00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:32.089
- Boxes are on the second floor.
- You're fucking kidding me.

440
00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:34.322
Derek, calm down.

441
00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.249
You blew him, didn't you?

442
00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.125
Like I need to stoop
to that level.

443
00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:44.451
Now... get the fuck
out of my face.

444
00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:46.364
I'm taking this to The Nine.

445
00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:49.842
Sure.
Good luck with that.

446
00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.849
And I want my mug back.

447
00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.929
♪♪

448
00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:57.368
The Nine, the company's
board of directors.

449
00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:01.002
Good morning, everybody.
This is the Vanda Corp file.

450
00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.401
DEREK: No one here goes up
or down without their vote.

451
00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:05.722
Rumor has it that they're
actually cybernetic organisms,

452
00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:08.121
but that hasn't been
officially confirmed yet.

453
00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:09.805
Now, there's
a common misconception

454
00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:12.042
about the death gesture
during gladiatorial combat.

455
00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.964
The actual phrase
used in Roman texts

456
00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:16.122
doesn't translate
as thumbs down,

457
00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:17.645
but rather thumbs turned.

458
00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:19.006
Personally, I think
we should hang,

459
00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:21.367
draw and quarter
the little fucker.

460
00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:25.525
But, you know, that's just me.
So let's vote.

461
00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:26.806
DEREK:
That's because the victors

462
00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:28.200
finished off their opponents

463
00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:29.964
with a sword thrust
across the throat.

464
00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:34.131
So it's unanimous.
Call Lester.

465
00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:37.602
DEREK: Enter Lester McGill,
head of human resources.

466
00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:40.366
No, not her.
That guy.

467
00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:44.161
♪♪

468
00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:46.163
He takes care
of the firm's layoffs.

469
00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:51.531
He's as cold as his methods are
efficient, a perfect fit here.

470
00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:55.048
Naturally,
we call him The Reaper,

471
00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:56.440
and he's the last person

472
00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:58.841
you want to see standing
at your doorway.

473
00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:01.002
♪♪

474
00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:04.482
Mind if I come in... Derek?

475
00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:06.324
DEREK: If I said no?

476
00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:08.482
Thank you.

477
00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:16.531
D-Do you even know
what happened?

478
00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:18.205
I don't care what happened.

479
00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.761
You must be good friends
with Kara, then.

480
00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:24.885
I hope she dies promptly.

481
00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.451
Glad we're on the same page.

482
00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:30.400
Urn, The Nine listen to you,
and I have proof that...

483
00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:31.886
- Sign here...
- ...this was not my mist--

484
00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.326
...and here.

485
00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:35.887
What the hell are you doing?

486
00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.804
My job.

487
00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:39.644
So you are on her side.

488
00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:43.282
I'm on the right side.
Always am.

489
00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.522
That's why it's me firing you.

490
00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.446
Fuck you.

491
00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:52.649
Sign these documents
from upstairs

492
00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:55.485
so I can clear accounting
to transfer your severance pay

493
00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.369
into your account.

494
00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:05.284
DEREK: Do you know what this is?

495
00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:07.010
This is a statement saying

496
00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.606
that I take full responsibility
over the Vanda Corp mess.

497
00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:13.088
I'll have to file that
under "N" for "not my problem."

498
00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:15.322
I could be disbarred.

499
00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.602
I could face legal action
from the client.

500
00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:19.444
I'm just the messenger, Derek.

501
00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:22.729
Yelling at me is like yelling at
your watch because you're late.

502
00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:24.689
Why would I sign this crap?

503
00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:27.446
♪♪

504
00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:29.045
To get rich.

505
00:22:29.240 --> 00:22:32.642
♪♪

506
00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:34.086
Wow.

507
00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:37.369
Glad to see we're now
on the same page.

508
00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:40.251
♪♪

509
00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:43.768
Glad to see I'm not.

510
00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:46.008
You want to do this
the hard way?

511
00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:48.891
I want to do this the right way.

512
00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:51.361
I want to speak with him
and The Nine.

513
00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:53.807
Executive decisions are
not subject to appeal.

514
00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:55.962
This one fucking better be

515
00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:58.964
because I'm not leaving this
building until I plead my case.

516
00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:00.007
Understood.

517
00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:01.321
[ Tapping ]

518
00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:09.520
♪♪

519
00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:11.571
[ Horn honking ]

520
00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:15.247
[ Siren wailing in distance ]

521
00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:17.641
[ Engine revs, tires screech ]

522
00:23:17.800 --> 00:23:20.167
[ Indistinct conversations ]

523
00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:28.320
